## **A.3.5 Timing for structures** 

_Classes_ are classifiers for things that exist in time ( _occurrences_ ), as compared to numbers or other mathematical entities. It usually matters when these things come into and go out of existence, at least relative to each other. For example, in structures it is typically intended that parts exist for at least as long as the thing they are part of. In the bicycle example above, the wheel atoms should exist at least as long as the bicycle atom. A simple way to do this is for a structure and its parts to all exist at exactly the same time, as show below. Bicycle is class with its part features subset from _`timeCoincidentOccurrences`_ , ensuring the values of `rollsOn` and `holdsWheel` happen (start and end) at exactly the same time as the bicycle occurrence they are part of, see 9.2.4.1 . 

