## **A.3.8 Timing for behavior, Changing feature values** 

This covers changes in feature values of occurrences. Change execution requires creating additional atoms for the periods ( _time slices_ ) when feature values are unchanged for each occurrence ( _life_ ), and ordering the slices in time as feature values change. Time slice atoms are also occurrences, but represent the same thing as their life occurrence, just for a potentially smaller period of time, see 9.2.4.1 . 

Changes to occurrence feature values is modeled using the library behavior _FeatureWritePerformance_ as a step, specifying when the change is to happen, see 9.2.8.1 . Time slices are created each time it is performed. 

